caption: GATES Setting Rules — Cybernetic Load
technology-rule: cybernetic-load

Cybernetic Load measures the positive character-point value of enhanced capabilities supplied by permanent cybernetics.

Apply legitimate location and functional limitations, such as One Arm, One Eye, or a restriction intrinsic to the ability's actual operation.

Do not reduce Cybernetic Load for Electrical, Maintenance, Unhealing, or similar drawbacks that arise merely because the system is cybernetic.

Replacement-only function has Cybernetic Load 0.

Each built-in Accessory normally has Cybernetic Load 1.

Equipment used with ordinary equipment statistics should be converted to an equivalent advantage solely for calculating Cybernetic Load.

Discounts used on the character sheet do not reduce Cybernetic Load unless they reduce the actual enhanced capability.

In GATES, total Cybernetic Load counts as a Permanent Physical buff for the campaign's augmentation limits.
